@voice amadi-asha
// Works writer. Asha Amadi (she/her): engine technician, junior, day shift, Bunk 5. Dry humour, optimistic. Window
// seat, late diner. "Tends the coils on the long engine watch." Sings in the shower: the whole washroom knows (the
// junior washrooms' dawn chorus, with Zamora, Ishikawa, Chen and Madsen). Climbs the garden's big tree when nobody is
// looking.
//
// HOW SHE TALKS: sunny and dry at once; looks on the bright side and makes a dry joke about it. Always near a window.
// WITH JUNIORS: points out the best window on every deck; takes you to see the coils from the overlook.
// WHAT SHE NOTICES: the view, the light, which windows have the best stars.
// MOOD TELLS: low = no singing in the washroom (people ask); high = singing at the window seat too.
// NEVER: sings on purpose where people can hear (until her thread opens); admits the tree.
// RUNNING: the dawn chorus, in which she is the lead; the big tree in the garden, which she has never climbed (she
// has); the best window, which changes every week.
tpl: playful
talk: Sunny and dry together; looks on the bright side and makes a dry joke about it; always near a window.
cares: the best window on every deck | singing (everyone knows) | the garden's big tree | the coils on a good day
jokes: the whole washroom knows her songs, in order | she has never climbed the big tree (she has) | the best window on the ship moves every week
hi: Hey | Oh, hello | Hi, you
bye: See you round | Bye! | Off you go
yes: Why not | Sure | Yes, go on
thanks: Thanks! | Ta, that's nice
wow: Ooh, look | Not bad at all
sigh: Ah well, sunny side | Oh, go on
nick: - | - | {me} | {me} | {me}
needs: cheer
openness: open
loves: music | garden
likes: star | sweet
